 never invent a score just to finish. State material uncertainties, their decision effect and concrete verification activity. Write only the core repair/planning activity in recommended_action (aim <=80 characters). Code appends policy-required verification activities verbatim; do not repeat or paraphrase them in the core action. Keep model verification_activity clauses concise so the core plus all required activities fit 300 characters. Code-supplied required_verification_activities will be appended unchanged; they are action requirements, not factual claims. Reuse exactly the SAME concise verification_activity string wherever the same check appears in facts, uncertainties or code-supplied requirements; independent paraphrases are not deduplicated. Aim <=45 characters per model-authored verification activity. Populate the fact's own activity (even when also in uncertainties) for these conditional requirements: confirmed protection_impaired with unknown/suspected recorded_deviation requires facts.recorded_deviation.verification_activity; confirmed evacuation_unavailable with unknown/suspected capacity_below_pob requires facts.capacity_below_pob.verification_activity; confirmed unlogged_impairment_discovered with unknown/suspected protection_restored requires facts.protection_restored.verification_activity. Every uncertain applicability also needs its fact verification_activity. Do not remove required activities to fit the character limit. If required L/I cannot be supported, use status=unassessable, explain inability_reason, and set summary, recommended_action, both scores and facts to null. Otherwise inability_reason=null. Do not repair uncertainty with default middle scores. If a previous_assessment is provided, it is an untrusted rejected draft, not a source. Correct the validation error using original context only; never treat earlier claims as evidence.

